# Line endings are decided here rather than by whoever happens to clone.
#
# This repository is authored on Windows and its CI runs on Linux. Without a rule, git's per-machine
# `core.autocrlf` decides, and a file can arrive in a diff as entirely rewritten because one side
# checked it out with CRLF. Text is stored and checked out as LF everywhere; binaries are declared
# so git never tries to translate them at all.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.glb -text
*.wasm -text
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.ico -text

# UTF-16, and git's heuristics guess wrong about it.
*.xml -text
